From e4162cd0f105601092d8266f79ed3b4b6d5cdbbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:31:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FBar kernels: modified tangent operator applied on the fly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tangent operator of the FBar formulation, `K' = α K + v ⊗ c` (`v = K
F`, `c = dα/dF`), was stored at the integration points (the square of the
number of components of the gradients, 81 values per point in 3D) in
addition to the tangent operator blocks of the behaviour. It is now
applied on the fly by the kernels of the stiffness matrices, which
multiply the tangent operator blocks by vectors: `K' x = α K x + v (c ·
x)`. Only `v` and `c` are stored (18 values per point in 3D, 63 values
less), which matters for large meshes (about 6 GB less for 12 million
integration points).

New optional argument of `addStiffnessMatrices`,
`addStiffnessMatricesDiagonals` and `addTangentOperatorAction`: the
scaling and update of rank one of the tangent operator blocks at each
point (`TangentOperatorModification`, deformation gradients only),
applied by `multiplyByTangentOperator` in the kernels (compiled only for
the deformation gradients). The functions of the FBar formulation take
the tangent operator blocks of the behaviour, and check that they are the
ones from which `v` and `c` were computed, and the sizes of the data.
